<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ's Ergo raises fixed mortgage rates.</title>
<headline>NZ's Ergo raises fixed mortgage rates.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMP subsidiary Ergo on Friday lifted its one-year fixed mortgage interest rates to 9.25 percent from 9.10 percent.</p>
<p>It lifted its two-year rate to 9.6 percent from 9.4 percent, and its three-year rate to 9.75 percent from 9.5 percent.</p>
<p>The floating rate remains unchanged at 9.4 percent.  </p>
<p>Ergo said the change followed recent increases in long-term interest rates on the wholesale money market.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
